addToken.t.sol
├── when caller is not the owner
│   └── it should revert with {OwnableUnauthorizedAccount} error
└── when caller is the owner
    ├── when token is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with {PERPEX__ZERO_ADDRESS} error
    ├── when oracle is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with {PERPEX__ZERO_ADDRESS} error
    ├── when token is already allowed
    │   └── it should revert with {PERPEX__INVALID_TOKEN} error
    └── when token and oracle are valid and token is not allowed yet
        ├── it should add the new token to the list of allowed tokens
        ├── it should add the corresponding oracle to the list of oracles
        └── it should emit the {TokenAdded} event
